Z||000000||GT Bastard||05-04-2000||01:45 AM||||I got my MSD coil already and installed it immediately.  My low rpm miss is now gone, and she revs clean!  I'm guessing I would have gotten similar results with a replacement OEM coil, but having the MSD is a piece of mind.  The existing coild looked factory...  The MSD coil was easy as hell to install.  Just plug and play!||||reg||14
Z||000001||1FST2M6||05-04-2000||02:20 PM||||now add a 6al and you'll notice just as much improvment yet again. anyone else have a MSD box? 6A, 6AL, BTM? after ditching my Crane Hi6s i droped in my 6BTM.. multi spark till 3200rpm then capacive discharge. Over 3200 it's a totaly different car.. sounds deeper pulls harder... only 4 lbft difference on the dyno from 3100 to 3200 but the botty-o-meter says its different. the capacity discharge unit that crane makes is nice but this is better. just one more thing to think about... <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 05-04-2000).]||||reg||1
